# Examples where no ignores are needed:
# If only source/config files like .sql, .py, .js, .java, .go, .cpp, .h, .md, .txt, .json, .yml, .yaml, .toml, .cfg, .ini are present

# In this case, only database.sql was modified, which is a source file
# No build artifacts, dependencies, or temp files detected in changes
# Therefore, no .gitignore rules are needed for this project state